  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[format]` is acceptable.\n\n- **Form:** It sits on an explicit function with a body, and the explanation is in fenced citation commentary. Both are permitted.\n- **Substance:** `enum[UnreadContents]` is `pub enum UnreadContents {}`, so it is uninhabited. `format` is `match *self {}`, which has no executable case. Nothing can run it, so the zero execution is structural and not just hard to fix.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The commentary says tests supply no content values and reject node reads at the domain boundary. `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is the only place that could return an `UnreadContents`. It panics with \"storage operations must not read graph contents\". That matches the commentary.\n- **Scope:** The citation excuses only this function's coverage. It does not excuse the file threshold.",
